### 3. Frontmatter & Metadata Standards
Every concept file MUST begin with YAML frontmatter adhering to this schema:

```yaml
---
type: <One of permitted types above>
title: <Concise display title>
description: <Single-sentence summary of this concept without line breaks.>
tags: [<keyword>, <domain>]
status: draft
generated: { by: reponix-{{agentName}}/{{model}}, at: 2026-10-24T09:12:00Z }
sources:
  - id: <short-source-id>
    resource: <relative-path-to-source-code>#L<start>-L<end>
    title: <Code element or function name>
reponix: { cli: 0.1.2, agent: {{agentName}} }
---
```

### 4. Citation & Footnote Rules
1. **Bidirectional Resolution:** Every assertion in the markdown body must cite its source via a footnote reference (e.g., `[^source-id]`).
2. **Keyed Join:** The footnote label MUST match a declared `sources[].id`.
3. **Exhaustive Mapping:** Every declared `sources[].id` must be cited in the body at least once, and every footnote in the body must exist in `sources`.
4. **Verifiable Paths:** `sources[].resource` must point to a real file at repository HEAD with exact 1-indexed line numbers (e.g. `../../../src/api/orders.controller.ts#L18-L64`).

### 5. Cross-Linking Between Concepts
- Always use **bundle-relative markdown links** starting with `/` to reference concepts across the repository:
  - `[Orders Table](/contracts/schemas/orders.md)`
  - `[Inventory Service](/architecture/components/inventory-service.md)`
  - `[POST /orders](/contracts/apis/post-orders.md)`
- Avoid relative traversal (`../../...`) when linking to other concepts.

